 "note": "Result digests (final score, possessions, kickoffs, injuries, opening receiver, team counters) of synthetic sample_teams() games under the kernel 2014.4 candidate. These synthetic fixtures carry no strength record (legacy anchor path). The candidate replaced the 2014.2/2014.3 digests in its own commit because Tier 1 items 2 (half-final clock), 4 (in-game injuries on the possession stream) and 5 (injury denominators) and the E1 home term (0.023) change results by design for every newly resolved game, including legacy packets; closed 2013 receipts are never rerun. A credit-only or display-only kernel must reproduce these digests; a kernel that deliberately changes results replaces this file in its own commit. Re-recorded again for the E1 second pass (September 30, 2026): the injury exposure is now the participation slot model alone (the recorded snap line keeps the named-player uplift), so an onset draw can no longer depend on attribution; 2 of the 40 legacy-path digests moved. Re-recorded again for the candidate's phase 2 (September 30, 2026): all 40 legacy-path digests moved because every possession now carries three append-only fields (fg_prob, punt, layout_resample); with those fields set aside, 37 of 40 games are identical to the phase 1 candidate and 3 (regular 10, regular 19, postseason 4) moved because one field-goal make flipped under the distance logistic of register item 18 (51, 43 and 38 yards); no legacy-path game drew a layout resample.",
